  "body": "## Disposition\nOriginal **unsolved, 5/5 substantive author turns**. No counterexample to the original homogeneous-space implication is claimed.\n\nAll new homogeneous-space theorems explicitly require a **smooth affine acting group and a smooth schematic/fppf homogeneous variety**. The positive stabilizer classes are: finite prime-to-characteristic stabilizers; all finite \u00e9tale stabilizers when H1(k,G)=1; all multiplicative-type stabilizers, including non-smooth ones; and smooth stabilizers with reductive identity component and prime-to-characteristic Weyl and component orders. The gerbe arguments preserve the full objects and underlying torsors where required.\n\nThe known perfect-field theorem is credited to Florence, and constant affine-group torsor descent over arbitrary fields to Florence\u2013Gille. Historical novelty of the partial results is unverified.\n\nThe final explicit wild cyclic algebra shows a nonconstant PGL_p torsor over the full Puiseux union, blocking a blanket object-surjectivity shortcut. It is defined over a Laurent field, and is **not an original counterexample**. General wild noncommutative, unipotent, wild-Weyl and broader acting-group cases remain unresolved.\n\n## Proof and review\n- [Current reviewed status](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/74617174ddfb3ea726cea343a4ba915613724bdc/problems/30004320_laurent_descent/REVIEWED_STATUS.md)\n- [Full result and exact remaining gap](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/74617174ddfb3ea726cea343a4ba915613724bdc/problems/30004320_laurent_descent/FINAL_RESULT.md)\n- [Primary-source map](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/74617174ddfb3ea726cea343a4ba915613724bdc/problems/30004320_laurent_descent/FINAL_SOURCE_MAP.md)\n- [Full independent source/proof review](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/74617174ddfb3ea726cea343a4ba915613724bdc/problems/30004320_laurent_descent/review/ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md)\n\nIndependent AI-assisted audit: PASS for all stated partials, no mandatory revision. All five author receipts replay: **128,694** exact assertions; independent controls add **8,664**. The audit checked 72 final/historical bindings, 11 primary PDFs and all 42 author raw blobs. Finite controls supplement the written proofs and are not formal certification or human peer review.\n\nRun `python verify_publication.py` in the target folder (Python 3 and SymPy). Optional `--source-dir` verifies the separately obtained sources; their raw PDFs and all imported records are excluded from this publication.\n\n## Preservation and diff\nAll **42 author files and 7 manifest-bound review files** are byte-preserved. Four additive publication files provide current status and portable verification. All 53 remote contents and raw Git blob hashes match the local publication packet. The only non-target change is rank388's QUEUE status/turn cells: queued0/5 \u2192 unsolved5/5.\n\nFirst parent is fresh main `efd29c05204703acca9a0860812f54b94fae54b1`; second parent preserves final author WIP `b08662a16499edf37f0c0eae850cfa00b7778ed6`. One draft PR for this problem; no merge or release requested.",
